From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 12:01:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Use the no-argument rotation shader option

Armada's Gamescope build carries the ROCKNIX rotation shader patch, whose
--use-rotation-shader option is a boolean flag rather than a valued option.
Only enable it when the session explicitly sets USE_ROTATION_SHADER=1.
---
 usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus b/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus
index ac1cc1f..9e776e1 100755
--- a/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus
+++ b/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@ if [ -z "$GAMESCOPECMD" ]; then
 
 	USE_ROTATION_SHADER_OPTION=""
-	if [ -n "$USE_ROTATION_SHADER" ] && gamescope_has_option "--use-rotation-shader"; then
-		USE_ROTATION_SHADER_OPTION="--use-rotation-shader $USE_ROTATION_SHADER"
+	if [ "$USE_ROTATION_SHADER" = "1" ] && gamescope_has_option "--use-rotation-shader"; then
+		USE_ROTATION_SHADER_OPTION="--use-rotation-shader"
 	fi
 
 	BACKEND_OPTION=""
-- 
2.50.1
